# Slice 1 — deep-research provider claude -p → in-session subagent
#           fan-out (in-session-subagent-migration minor)

2026-06-02. First slice of the in-session-subagent-migration minor
per `docs/plans/claude-p-to-insession-subagent-fanout.md` §5
AC.RES1.*. Owner-greenlit (Luke, TG 13481) as the lowest-risk first
slice; it also sets up the post-June-15 live billing test.

MOTIVE (economic). Post-June-15-2026 `claude -p` / Agent-SDK usage
draws from a separate metered Agent SDK credit; in-session
subagents (the Task primitive a live Claude Code session uses) are
accounted against the subscription plan limits. This slice swaps the
SPAWN PRIMITIVE of the deep-research provider's production
ResearchSource — not the swarm shape, not the budget, not the
graceful-degradation contract.

Single-component fence on `framework/workspace-bootstrap/`. The
conversion lands entirely inside
`deep_role_research_provider.py` (+ one user-facing notice doc +
the AC.RES1.* tests):

  - NEW: an in-session dispatcher seam — a process-level registry
    (`set_in_session_dispatcher` / `get_in_session_dispatcher` /
    `clear_in_session_dispatcher`) the live host session wires with
    its Task-primitive dispatcher callable
    `(prompt: str, *, model: str) -> str`. The standalone Python
    provider is NOT itself a Claude session; the live session that
    runs onboarding registers the dispatcher. No dispatcher
    registered → graceful fallback (the same degrade path the old
    `claude` -absent case took).

  - NEW: `InSessionResearchSource` — the production ResearchSource.
    Builds the SAME bounded research prompt, dispatches it through
    the registered in-session dispatcher, and parses the result
    through the UNCHANGED `_parse_research_envelope`. No detached
    `claude -p` subprocess; no `spawn_isolated_claude` call; no
    Anthropic SDK / `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` (subscription-routed via the
    host session's own auth). On no-dispatcher / dispatch-raise /
    unparseable-result → `ResearchUnavailableError` → the
    AC.DRRGRACE.1 fallback.

  - CHANGED: `make_default_research_provider` now constructs the
    provider with the `InSessionResearchSource` as the production
    default (was `ClaudeSubagentResearchSource`).

  - KEPT (NOT deleted): `ClaudeSubagentResearchSource` (the residual
    `claude -p` mechanism) + its `spawn_isolated_claude` call.
    `loam_spawn_isolation`'s scope narrows to residual-only; the
    converted in-session path never touches it (no subprocess argv
    to isolate). Narrated in-code so a future reader does not "clean
    up" a still-load-bearing guard (the residual `-p` path + the
    launchd-sessionless path still need it).

  - NEW user-facing surface:
    `docs/insession-subagent-keep-open-notice.md` — the plain-
    language "keep loam open in the background to finish while
    you're away; close it and it pauses" notice (AC.RES1.5).

