Method-level choices (builder's call per ODD §1.1):

  - D-build.1 (dispatcher as an injected callable via a process-
    level registry): the live host session — the only context with
    the Task primitive — registers a `(prompt, *, model) -> str`
    dispatcher. A registry (not a constructor arg threaded through
    the whole intake) lets the production
    `make_default_research_provider()` resolve the dispatcher at
    call time without N call sites passing it down. No-registration
    is the natural degrade trigger (AC.RES1.3), mirroring the old
    `claude` -absent degrade.

  - D-build.2 (keep `ClaudeSubagentResearchSource`): the `-p` source
    stays as the residual mechanism so the spawn-isolation guard
    stays exercised + load-bearing for the launchd-sessionless
    residual path. Deleting it would re-expose that path's spawns
    to the proven Telegram kill vector (plan §3 Surface #3 / H-3).

  - D-build.3 (notice as a standalone doc): a top-level
    `docs/insession-subagent-keep-open-notice.md` is reachable
    through the normal docs path (vs buried in a code comment),
    satisfying AC.RES1.5's "reachable through the normal user-
    facing path" + the cold-walk outcome-altitude check.

